# Local pull of our own published library, for testing the developer-facing
# loop against real Figma data. `spec-layer pull` writes .speclayer/ and
# `spec-layer init` writes speclayer.json; both are working files here, not
# repo content. A consumer repo WOULD commit speclayer.json (it carries the
# library id, never the pull key) — this repo is the publisher, not a consumer.
.speclayer/
speclayer.json

# The prose tree, the internal vault, the marketing site, and the capture
# library now live in a separate private repository, so the ignore rules that
# covered their generated archives and delivery variants went with them.

# Local design notes. The prose tree proper lives in the private repository;
# this is a scratch space for a spec written alongside a branch.
docs/
